<iscomment>
    Places the in-grid banner in a product grid.

    Included by both grid templates right after their tile loop, with one page scoped
    variable set above it:

      tsGridBanner   result of topsortBanners.getGridBannerPlacement:
                     { slotId, row, categoryId, searchQuery }

    The banner is the last element of the grid in the markup, not an element between the
    tiles of two rows. The HITES stylesheet spaces the tiles with nth-child rules, which count
    every sibling, so an element inserted between two tiles would shift the margins of every
    tile after it. Here the tiles keep their place and the stylesheet moves the banner up
    with flex order: the banner is order 1 and every cell below its row is order 2, through
    the ts-grid-below-banner--* classes the loop gives them.

    The same remote include as every other banner slot, so the grid keeps whatever page
    caching it has. preserveWrapper keeps the wrapper in the document when no bid wins: it is
    hidden, and a hidden last element changes nothing in the grid.
</iscomment>
<div class="ts-banner-slot ts-banner-slot--grid ts-banner-slot--${tsGridBanner.slotId}">
    <isinclude url="${URLUtils.url('Topsort-Banner', 'slotId', tsGridBanner.slotId, 'cgid', tsGridBanner.categoryId || '', 'q', tsGridBanner.searchQuery || '', 'preserveWrapper', 'true')}" />
</div>
